Let a service name its container

Services accept an optional "container" field (stripped, at most 64
characters, stored only when set) naming the Docker container that runs
them, for when it differs from the service's id or name. It is passed
through /api/config and the dashboard's service views ("" when unset), so
image updates can be matched to services.

